          "quote": "Generally a charge of 50-100 g is used for directional solidification. The alloy is prepared from high purity (more than 99.99% pure) elements by induction levitation melting in the same segmented water-cooled copper crucible [ 1,2] that is used for directional solidification. The alloys are melted at least twice, and in most cases three times or more, in order to ensure homogeneity prior to directional solidification.",
